  clock: 3  # 80cc
  nonce: 80cc  # 80cc
  message: "Closing as done. The work was completed in commit 4fc0cff999 (refactor(framework_patterns): WI-fojun — Pattern.framework_role field + shim removal, 2026-05-06):\n\n1. Added `Pattern.framework_role` field with its own `_framework_role_re` matcher (parallel to `symbol_kind`).\n2. `Pattern.matches()` updated to AND `symbol_kind:` and `framework_role:` when both are specified; either can be specified independently.\n3. Backward-compat fall-back-to-meta['framework_role']-when-symbol_kind-regex-doesn't-match shim REMOVED. The 'fall back to meta when symbol.kind doesn't match' branch at the former lines 396-401 and 423-428 no longer exists.\n4. Four YAMLs migrated to use `framework_role:` field: laravel.yaml, phoenix.yaml, rails.yaml, sinatra.yaml.\n5. `test_pattern_matches_symbol_kind` updated to exercise the new field. 100% coverage on framework_patterns.py preserved.\n\nTracker drift caused this item to remain todo_soft for 5 days — the commit closed the work but the tracker update was missed.\n\nResidual gap (filed as a NEW item if not already): 18 unfolded `symbol_kind:` references remain in config-conventions.yaml (13), language-conventions.yaml (4), library-exports.yaml (1). These reference kinds that were folded in Wave 6 (Cluster B/G) but to non-framework_role meta keys (`config_format`, `dependency_scope`, `package_ecosystem`, `entry_role`) rather than framework_role. The Pattern matcher currently only supports `symbol_kind:`, `framework_role:`, `decorator:`, `base_class:`, etc. — not general meta-key matching. Migrating these YAMLs needs Pattern to grow new meta-key fields (or a generalized meta query mechanism). Out of scope for WI-fojun (which was specifically about the framework_role fold residue from Cluster D and the WI-habut Wave 5 PRs). Filing separately."  # 80cc
